/nicon-relay
*.db
*.exe
/webspace/config.local.php
/.env
/node_modules/
/playwright-report/
/test-results/
# Defense-in-depth against a real production DB dump ending up in a commit
# (this already happened once this session — never staged, purely by
# operator diligence, not because anything stopped it). Doesn't affect the
# one .sql file actually meant to be tracked (webspace/schema.sql) — an
# already-tracked file stays tracked regardless of a later-added ignore
# rule; this only keeps a NEW .sql file from being swept in by `git add -A`.
*.sql
!/webspace/schema.sql
